# SOC Investigation Report: Suspected Phishing Email

## 1. Incident Summary

**Incident Type:** Suspected Phishing
**Investigation Level:** SOC Analyst Level 1
**Affected User:** John Doe
**Impersonated Organisation:** Microsoft
**Investigation Status:** Preliminary Investigation
**Classification:** Suspected Malicious Email

## 2. Incident Description

An email was presented to the user, John Doe, claiming that his Microsoft 365 account would be suspended unless he verified his login credentials.

The email contained urgent language and a suspicious verification link. The sender used a domain resembling Microsoft's brand name.

The objective of this investigation was to identify potential phishing indicators and assess the security risk associated with the email.

## 3. Evidence Collected

The following indicators were identified from the supplied email sample:

| Evidence                  | Observed Information                                                                  |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Sender Address            | [security-alert@micros0ft-security.com](mailto:security-alert@micros0ft-security.com) |
| Sender Domain             | micros0ft-security.com                                                                |
| Subject                   | URGENT: Your Microsoft 365 Account Will Be Suspended                                  |
| Impersonated Organisation | Microsoft                                                                             |
| Suspicious URL            | micros0ft-security.example/verify                                                     |
| Recipient                 | John Doe                                                                              |

## 4. Technical Analysis

### 4.1 Sender and Domain Analysis

The sender domain contains a character substitution, using the number zero (0) in place of the letter 'o' in Microsoft.

This resembles a domain impersonation technique commonly associated with phishing attacks.

### 4.2 Email Content Analysis

The email uses urgent language, warning the recipient that their Microsoft 365 account will be suspended.

This creates pressure on the recipient to act quickly without properly examining the legitimacy of the message.

### 4.3 URL Analysis

The email contains a suspicious verification URL:

micros0ft-security.example/verify

The URL uses a domain that resembles Microsoft's branding.

The supplied URL uses the reserved `.example` top-level domain. Therefore, it is treated as a training indicator and has not been established as a live malicious website.

### 4.4 Email Authentication

SPF, DKIM and DMARC results were not available in the supplied evidence.

Further examination of the original email headers would be required to establish whether the message passed or failed these authentication checks.

